<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Driver GPS data notice · Hambelela</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../assets/css/delivery-tracking.css"></head><body class="delivery-tracking"><main class="tracking-card" style="max-width:760px;margin:32px auto"><h1>Driver GPS data notice</h1><p>This describes the Hambelela company-phone tracking software. The Owner must explain and authorise its workplace use with the employee before pairing a phone.</p><h2>What is collected</h2><p>During configured work hours, the phone sends GPS coordinates, observation times and accuracy to the Hambelela portal. Device connection status, battery level and app version help identify interruptions. The phone displays a persistent notification while its tracking service runs; the user can stop it.</p><h2>Access and purpose</h2><p>The registered phone is linked to an existing Driver employee. Fleet GPS and history are Owner-only and are used to oversee deliveries. Phone credentials do not grant access to employee accounts, customer payments or the rest of the portal. Location evidence does not automatically create penalties or performance deductions.</p><h2>Working hours and interruptions</h2><p>No new GPS is requested outside the configured working window. GPS also stops when the server authorisation expires after an hour without contact. Android permissions, battery controls, phone shutdown or network outages can interrupt tracking; an old location is not proof of the current location.</p><h2>Retention</h2><p>Server GPS retention defaults to 30 days and can be configured by the Owner from 1 to 90 days. Expired observations are removed by the hourly retention job. The encrypted phone queue accepts observations for upload for 24 hours only; expired local entries are cleaned when the app processes its queue. Audit entries identifying administrative changes are kept separately and do not contain access secrets.</p><h2>Google Maps features</h2><p>The Owner dashboard uses Google Maps. Viewing the map or requesting a road estimate can share map-view coordinates, the current Driver position and the selected delivery address with Google. The portal limits billable server requests and does not archive Google route geometry or travel estimates. Geocoded coordinates are retained for fewer than 30 days.</p><p>Use of Google Maps features is subject to the <a href="https://maps.google.com/help/terms_maps.html" rel="noopener">Google Maps/Google Earth Additional Terms of Service</a> and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>. Google estimates are not guaranteed arrival times.</p><h2>Questions or corrections</h2><p>Contact the Hambelela Owner or authorised administrator to review the linked employee, working hours, retention settings or disputed delivery evidence. Do not send passwords or device pairing codes in public messages.</p><p><a href="index.php">Return to Delivery</a></p></main></body></html>
